{
  "note": [
    "The Waiting Area's fabric (DR-106), cut from the one Kalamontee layout in scripts/fabric-kalamontee.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. WAITING-AREA.metadata.json v4: 12 x 4 x 8, the eye at the middle, concrete.",
    "The game: \"This is a concrete platform sparsely furnished with benches. The platform continues to the east, and to the south is a metal door.\" (compone.zil 3155-3158) -- a fixed LDESC with no ACTION routine, so nothing here ever changes but the door. Three benches in a row 1.3 m off the north wall, out of both travel lanes.",
    "East, the 4.0 x 2.6 portal onto the Kalamontee Platform with the deck running unbroken through it: its far wall 22.2 m out, the sign's pale panel on it, and through the portal's south edge the east 4.96 m of the Alfie berth's 6.0, with the whole 2.6 m of the car's own doorway inside it. The car itself is not cut here -- scripts/fabric-shuttle.mjs cuts the shuttles -- so the berth is drawn empty and the room's ALFIE-BERTH state waits on that file. South, the red metal door, shut in the base; open (LOWER-ELEVATOR-DOOR has OPENBIT, which here can only mean the car is down) the lit car 2.18 m off with its control panel on its east wall."
